LanternBoy: {
	// DisplayName: The Lantern Boy
	// Origin: Those who walk the mountain road at night tell of a lantern waiting at its end with no one beneath it. One traveler braved a longer look — and when he came to, he was the one looking out from inside the lamp
	// Power: 「Guiding Light」Three Ghost Lanterns orbit the bearer, their shadows echoing Onikiri's normal slashes off-beat for a combined sixty percent of its power.
	// DeathReason: "{0} became the one inside the fourth lantern"
}

CrimsonBride: {
	// DisplayName: The Crimson Bride
	// Origin: A bridal palanquin once stood at somebody's gate with no bearers to carry it, and stood there seven nights. On the eighth night someone lifted the curtain — and from then on, the palanquin answered to a new bride
	// Power: 「The Procession」Press the Self-Restart key and the palanquin comes following your trail of blood, carrying the blade-bearer into an empty wedding hall; at the nuptial toast, wounds and afflictions alike are restarted.
	// DeathReason: "{0} boarded that palanquin"
}

ScapeGhost: {
	// DisplayName: The Scapegoat Wraith
	// Origin: It left no name behind in life; it only remembers dying in other people's places, so many times it forgot which death was its own. The day it was entered into the register, its birth date was written beside your name — from then on, your death is its to take
	// Power: 「Death's Stand-In」At the instant death arrives, it seizes a life from afar and forces your death into that body
	// DeathReason: "{0} died in its place, this once"
}

HeadlessShade: {
	// DisplayName: The Headless Shade
	// Origin: On a night of swaying lamplight, a man looked down and saw his shadow twitch when he had not moved — and looking closer, there was nothing above its shoulders. Something that lost its head had moved into a living man's shadow
	// Power: 「Dismember」It lurks behind you, then rushes anything living and tears its body into pieces
	// DeathReason: "{0} was torn into pieces by their own shadow"
}

GhostHand: {
	// DisplayName: The Charred Hand
	// Origin: A charred, withered arm, burnt through and still gripping hard. No one knows whose it once was; all anyone knows is that it reaches for whatever lives
	// Power: 「Grip」A withered hand lashes out from behind to seize prey, pinning it down and crushing it over and over; when prey abounds, more hands reach out — even colossal beings cannot slip its fingers
	// DeathReason: "{0} was dragged into the wall"
}

GhostRain: {
	// DisplayName: The Ghost Rain
	// Origin: Everyone caught in that rain says the same thing: look up, and it is not clouds — it is faces, pressing down layer upon layer. The drops do not hurt when they land; it is just that every one feels like someone claiming you
	// Power: 「Ghost Rain」While equipped and Onikiri is held, the gloom stays and the ghost rain pours; living things caught in the veil are slowly eaten away, or dragged up into the rain
	// DeathReason: "{0} was claimed by the rain"
}

System: {
	// ScapeGhostActivated: 「Death's Stand-In」— {0} bore this death in your place
	// ScapeGhostUnknownTarget: something living
	// ScapeGhostDeathBroadcast: "{0} took the hit for {1} — {2}"
	// ErosionCrawl: Something is crawling beneath the skin
	// ErosionStain: A corpse-blue tinge creeps up the fingertips
	// ErosionMirror: The thing in the mirror does not quite look like you
	// RevivalStir: The name on the talisman shifted
	// RevivalRise: It is watching you through the paper
	// RevivalBrink: The talisman is too hot to hold
	// RevivalHudBrink: One more use and it wakes
}

Coven: {
	// RainHandName: Reach From The Rain
	// RainHandNote: Soaked prey no longer sits beyond arm's reach — the withered hand hangs down from the rainline above it. Up to five hands reach out at once in the rain, and the crush grows heavier with the downpour
	// RainShadeName: Wet Edge
	// RainShadeNote: While the wound the shade tore is still open, every tick of rain-rot on that target is doubled
	// HandShadeName: Held Down, Then Cut
	// HandShadeNote: The shade goes for prey the withered hand has hold of first — its speed is already pinned to zero, so the strike cannot miss
	// LanternHandName: Seen By Lanternlight
	// LanternHandNote: Prey the lantern has lit can be found by the hand even through cover; lantern slashes land 60% heavier on a target already held
	// BrideName: Wedding Hall
	// BrideNote: Prey drawn into the hall at the cup-sharing frame keeps every other mark on it from fading until the hall breaks up
	// ScapeName: Take The Blow
	// ScapeNote: Each time the substitute dies, every other wraith on the wheel drops one step of revival
	// CallName: Calling Each Other
	// CallNote: Wraiths sharing the wheel wake one another: use any of them and the rest gain a little revival. This holds even between two with no signature reaction
	// BurstName: Three Marks Break
	// BurstNote: When three different marks meet on one target, they detonate together as a single hit, and every wraith involved pays one revival
}
